{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/960250-open-call-beast-dark-era-idea-classical-greece","id":960250,"title":"[Open Call] Beast Dark Era Idea - Classical Greece","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-29T22:51:46-07:00","id":960250,"title":"[Open Call] Beast Dark Era Idea - Classical Greece","content":"So I've tossed this idea around elsewhere in pieces and parts, but figured taking it to the experts here on the game's home forum might be the best bet: a Dark Era for Beast set in the distant (possibly semi-mythical) past of Greece. The Beasts of this Era are divided between those who view themselves as divine messengers and deliverers of Olympian judgment (a la The Furies) and those who merely feed without a second thought towards reason or excuse. While similar to those in the modern day who espouse the idea of Lessons and teaching, there's an elevated sense of importance; even as they take the roles of holy judges of hubris, they themselves act as though they have the authority of the gods behind them.<br /> <br /> There are a few easy avenues for crossover here, with Mage as the most obvious one (laying the roots for <i>To The Strongest</i>), but an interesting potential for unique stories in Changeling and possible Deviant as well; that of the mortal cursed by the gods. Whether you look to those fairly punished by the Olympians (Arachne's pride in her weaving skill leading to her existence as a spider-monster), those unfairly judged (Medusa sometimes being described as being cursed by Athena for being raped in one of her temples), or those just caught in the schemes of the gods (the Minotaur had nothing to do with the punishment of his birth being laid on King Minos), there are a variety of supernatural beings in Mythic Greece changed by the touch of the divine. You then end up with an interesting dichotomy: the Beasts who believe themselves servants of the gods without proof, and those forever changed by the gods (or Fae masquerading as them, or sinister mystery cults that create Deviants) who resent their cursed state. Do you look to the obvious kinship between your monstrous self and these beings, or do you double down on your self-appointed purpose and cast them out as fair and deserving of their conditions?<br /> <br /> I figure I'd open this up to everyone on the Beast forum to either relentlessly mock or (hopefully) contribute to, as I'm rolling into the unique hell that is a retail holiday season <i>and</i> have a neglected 1960s America Mage setting to work on. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T00:38:11-07:00","id":960280,"title":"","content":"It's definitely a good setting for Beasts. I think it might be better to narrow it down to a specific era though - maybe the Athenian Golden Age, Athens was almost like a Tyrant in itself.<br /> <br /> I feel if anything it might be better to explore another line than Mage, if only because it already has its own Greek setting as you mentioned, albeit a later one. Changeling is a very clever idea - I'm reminded of the story of Arachne and how she could be seen as an example of a Beast Changeling. Geist could be a good fit too, with people like Orpheus and Heracles making day trips to the underworld. And of course while maybe not worth exploring to the same extant, I imagine the Muses from Promethean would be around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:09:54-07:00","id":960480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/960250-open-call-beast-dark-era-idea-classical-greece?p=960280#post960280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely a good setting for Beasts. I think it might be better to narrow it down to a specific era though - maybe the Athenian Golden Age, Athens was almost like a Tyrant in itself..</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're going mythic Greece, it should be set about a thousand years earlier.<br /> <br /> Obviously Echidna has to be mentioned seeing as how she is pretty much the Dark Mother. As for Typhon, the Father of Monsters, I think he should be the biggest, baddest Apex in Greece, and possibly the world. He could be alive or dead, but either way, Beasts would probably admire and fear him. I imagine he'd be trying/tried to become the Apex of all of Greece in the hopes of attracting the Dark Mother's attention. Beasts who idolized Typhon would believe that giving into their monstrous nature was what they were meant to do. Those that tried to rationalize it would probably say something about how it cleared out the weak and forced the strong to rise to the challenge. If I remember correctly, in Greek mythology Echidna was kept alive for so long so she could birth monsters to give heroes something to test themselves against.<br /> <br /> I think this would predate the Dream becoming too crowded, so we would probably have to cover what Heroes did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T23:56:29-07:00","id":961485,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking about this when you mentioned it in the /wodg/. Hercules was actually pretty stand up, as far as Greek Heroes go. I would want to see some Heroes that take after Hercules, and try to defend Greece from darkness.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see Beasts that take on less &quot;monstrous&quot; roles. Honestly I feel like Beast is way too confined to that role. I mean, what about things like the Pegasus (which was a child of Medusa)?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/960250-open-call-beast-dark-era-idea-classical-greece?p=960480#post960480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously Echidna has to be mentioned seeing as how she is pretty much the Dark Mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Dark Mother is <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Luna</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/a